<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Loss Functions for Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in the main text, introducing stochastic variables <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\hat{U}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\hat{U}}}</annotation></semantics></math> into the discriminative model requires marginalizing them back out in order to compute the loss, (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In III-A Logistic Forward-Forward ‣ III Theory ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), or its gradient.
The loss itself can be written as</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathcal{L}}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\frac{1}{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\frac{1}{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\frac{1}{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\hat{u}_{l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{Z}},{\bm{V}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\hat{u}_{l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}},\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathcal{L}}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\frac{1}{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\frac{1}{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\frac{1}{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\hat{u}_{l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{Z}},{\bm{V}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\hat{u}_{l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The expectation under <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> could be approximated by a sample average, except that computing the normalizer for this distribution is computationally intractable.
Instead we can interpret the penultimate line as an importance sampler, with <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as the proposal distribution and <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒖</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>
as the importance weight.
This is tractable because <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> factorizes ((<a href="#S3.E8" title="In III-B Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ III Theory ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>)), so samples can be drawn independently.
In terms of the importance weight, the normalizer can be written as</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)=\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒖</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right)=\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Putting (<a href="#A1.E15" title="In Appendix A Loss Functions for Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E16" title="In Appendix A Loss Functions for Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) together with an explicit expression for
<math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{(\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{l}}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right))}/\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒗</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{(\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{l}}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{v}}{}}}\right))}/\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathcal{L}}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\frac{{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(a_{l}-{\hat{U}}_{l}}}\right){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}|{\bm{V}}{}}}}{{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}|{\bm{V}}{}}}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathcal{L}}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\frac{{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(a_{l}-{\hat{U}}_{l}}}\right){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}|{\bm{V}}{}}}}{{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}|{\bm{V}}{}}}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In our experiments, however, we did not achieve competitive results with this importance sampler.
Alternatively, then, we can attempt to minimize the following upper bound:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{J}&amp;\mathrel{\vbox{\hbox{\scriptsize.}\hbox{\scriptsize.}}}=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}},{\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}\\
&amp;=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}\\
&amp;=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)}}\right\}\\
&amp;={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}+C.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>
<span class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_bottom"> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">.</span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">.</span></span> 
</span></mtext><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>p</mi><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>p</mi><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>p</mi><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{J}&amp;\mathrel{\vbox{\hbox{\scriptsize.}\hbox{\scriptsize.}}}=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}},{\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}\\
&amp;=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}\\
&amp;=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)}}\right\}\\
&amp;={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}+C.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This is (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In III-B Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ III Theory ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) in the main text.
It is an upper bound on the relative entropy in (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In III-A Logistic Forward-Forward ‣ III Theory ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) because it can be expressed as the sum of that relative entropy and another relative entropy:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{J}&amp;=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{Z}},{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}\\
&amp;=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}+\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{Z}},{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>p</mi><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>p</mi><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{J}&amp;=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{Z}},{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}\\
&amp;=\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{p\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}+\KL\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\{\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\middle\|\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{\hat{U}}}|{\bm{Z}},{\bm{V}}}}\right)}}\right\}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To compute the gradient of the joint relative entropy, (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In Appendix A Loss Functions for Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), with respect to the <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> row <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> of the input matrix <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{{W}}_{\text{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{{W}}_{\text{in}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we exploit the independence of the elements of <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\hat{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\hat{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> and consider <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{u}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{u}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> separately from the remaining elements, <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathcal{J}}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}&amp;=-\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\sum_{\hat{u}_{l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\hat{u}_{l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},\hat{u}_{l}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(a_{l}\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},{\hat{U}}_{l}=1}}\right)+(1-a_{l})\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},{\hat{U}}_{l}=0}}\right)}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[-\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},{\hat{U}}_{l}=1}}\right)+\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},{\hat{U}}_{l}=0}}\right)}}\right]a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathcal{J}}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}&amp;=-\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\sum_{\hat{u}_{l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\hat{u}_{l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},\hat{u}_{l}}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;=-{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(a_{l}\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},{\hat{U}}_{l}=1}}\right)+(1-a_{l})\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},{\hat{U}}_{l}=0}}\right)}}\right)}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[-\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},{\hat{U}}_{l}=1}}\right)+\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\bm{Z}}|\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l},{\hat{U}}_{l}=0}}\right)}}\right]a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The expectation can be carried out explicitly (third line) and differentiated (fourth line) because <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{U}}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{U}}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> has only two possible values.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The bracketed quantity on the last line of (<a href="#A1.E18" title="In Appendix A Loss Functions for Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) is the increase in surprisal when the <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> element of <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\hat{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\hat{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> is flipped from 0 to 1.
From the definition of the model output, (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In III-B Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ III Theory ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), the surprisal itself is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}}}\right)=A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\mathbf{{W}}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}}}\right)-{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}^{\text{T}}\mathbf{{W}}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}-\log(h({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒖</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒖</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mtext>T</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒖</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}{}|{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}{}}}\right)=A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\mathbf{{W}}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}}}\right)-{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}^{\text{T}}\mathbf{{W}}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{u}}-\log(h({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">so the increase in surprisal is</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sum_{d\neq l}^{{D}}\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{d}}+\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}}}\right)-A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sum_{d\neq l}^{{D}}\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{d}}}}\right)-{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>out</mtext><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>out</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>out</mtext><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mtext>T</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>out</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sum_{d\neq l}^{{D}}\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{d}}+\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}}}\right)-A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sum_{d\neq l}^{{D}}\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{d}}}}\right)-{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\bm{z}}^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Now recall from (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In III Theory ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In III Theory ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) that the readout weights are inversely proportional to the hidden dimension <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus for large numbers of hidden units, the difference of log-partition functions in (<a href="#A1.E19" title="In Appendix A Loss Functions for Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) approaches the directional derivative.
To make this explicit, we introduce unscaled weights <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\bar{w}}^{d}_{\text{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>out</mtext><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\bar{w}}^{d}_{\text{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}=\bm{\bar{w}}^{d}_{\text{out}}/{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>out</mtext><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>out</mtext><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}=\bm{\bar{w}}^{d}_{\text{out}}/{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then as the size of the hidden dimension grows large, the difference becomes</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lim_{{D}\to\infty}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sum_{d\neq l}^{{D}}\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{d}}+\frac{1}{{D}}\bm{\bar{w}}^{l}_{\text{out}}}}\right)-A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sum_{d\neq l}^{{D}}\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{d}}}}\right)}{1/{D}}\frac{1}{{D}}}}\right]=\frac{\partial{A}}{\partial{\bm{\eta}{}}}\cdot\bm{\bar{w}}^{l}_{\text{out}}\frac{1}{{D}}=\frac{\partial{A}}{\partial{\bm{\eta}{}}}\cdot\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>out</mtext><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>out</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>out</mtext><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝜼</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>out</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝜼</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>out</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{{D}\to\infty}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\frac{A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sum_{d\neq l}^{{D}}\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{d}}+\frac{1}{{D}}\bm{\bar{w}}^{l}_{\text{out}}}}\right)-A\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\sum_{d\neq l}^{{D}}\bm{w}^{d}_{\text{out}}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}u_{d}}}}\right)}{1/{D}}\frac{1}{{D}}}}\right]=\frac{\partial{A}}{\partial{\bm{\eta}{}}}\cdot\bm{\bar{w}}^{l}_{\text{out}}\frac{1}{{D}}=\frac{\partial{A}}{\partial{\bm{\eta}{}}}\cdot\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Substituting this quantity into the difference of surprisals (<a href="#A1.E19" title="In Appendix A Loss Functions for Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and thence into the gradient (<a href="#A1.E18" title="In Appendix A Loss Functions for Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathcal{J}}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}&amp;\approx{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\frac{\partial{A}}{\partial{\bm{\eta}}}-{\bm{Z}}}}\right)^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;\approx{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\frac{\partial{A}}{\partial{\bm{\eta}}}-{\bm{Z}}}}\right)^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}|{\bm{V}}}{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\hat{Z}}}{}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[{\bm{\hat{Z}}}\middle|{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}}}\right]}\middle|{\bm{V}}{}}}\right]}-{\bm{Z}}}}\right)^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}|{\bm{V}}}{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\psi\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\mathbf{{W}}_{\text{out}}{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)\middle|{\bm{V}}{}}}\right]}-{\bm{Z}}}}\right)^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mfrac><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mtext>in</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝜼</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒁</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>T</mtext></msup><mi>𝒘</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝜼</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒁</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>T</mtext></msup><mi>𝒘</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒁</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>T</mtext></msup><mi>𝒘</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒁</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>T</mtext></msup><mi>𝒘</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\mathcal{J}}}{\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{in}}}}&amp;\approx{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}_{\backslash l}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\frac{\partial{A}}{\partial{\bm{\eta}}}-{\bm{Z}}}}\right)^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;\approx{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\sum_{\bm{\hat{u}}{}}\hat{p}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\bm{\hat{u}}|{\bm{V}}}}\right)\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\frac{\partial{A}}{\partial{\bm{\eta}}}-{\bm{Z}}}}\right)^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}|{\bm{V}}}{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\hat{Z}}}{}|{\bm{\hat{U}}}}{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[{\bm{\hat{Z}}}\middle|{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}}}\right]}\middle|{\bm{V}}{}}}\right]}-{\bm{Z}}}}\right)^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}\\
&amp;={\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left\langle{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\hat{U}}}{}|{\bm{V}}}{\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left[\psi\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\mathbf{{W}}_{\text{out}}{\bm{\hat{U}}}}}\right)\middle|{\bm{V}}{}}}\right]}-{\bm{Z}}}}\right)^{\text{T}}\bm{w}^{l}_{\text{out}}a_{l}(1-a_{l}){\bm{V}}}}}\right\rangle_{{\bm{Z}}{},{\bm{V}}{}}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.5" class="ltx_p">The second line follows because, for a large number of hidden units, omitting or retaining a single row <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\bar{w}}^{l}_{\text{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>out</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\bar{w}}^{l}_{\text{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> does not much affect the gradient of the log-partition function.
The final lines follow, as in (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In III-A Logistic Forward-Forward ‣ III Theory ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), by substituting either the expectation of the sufficient statistics (penultimate line), or the inverse link (<math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\cdot}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\cdot}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>) applied to the natural parameters (final line), for the gradient of the log-partition function.
This is (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In III-B Binary Stochastic Forward-Forward ‣ III Theory ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) in the main text.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Energy consumption: a comparison of multiplication and memory operations</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notation Disclaimer*</span>
The notation used in this appendix is defined within the local context of this section and may differ from or be independent of the notation used in the main text.
Readers should interpret symbols and definitions as specific to this appendix to avoid any confusion.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In order to calculate the energy savings netted by the use of our binary stochastic forward-forward (BSFF) algorithm, here we make explicit how memory and multiplication operations scale with network parameters for each of BSFF, CwC-FF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, and backprop.
For simplicity, we consider the same architecture in all cases.
This architecture consists of <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers, with each layer containing the following sublayers:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">convolution</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">activation</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">max pooling</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">batch normalization</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We assume a simple Von-Neumann computational model, comprising memory units and compute units, as shown abstractly in Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ No–BatchNorm Case ‣ B-C Forward Forward Algorithm (BSN): Number of Multiplications and Memory Accesses ‣ Appendix B Energy consumption: a comparison of multiplication and memory operations ‣ Energy-Efficient Supervised Learning with aBinary Stochastic Forward-Forward Algorithm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Although Forward–Forward–based algorithms can benefit from more advanced architectures that exploit multi–level memory hierarchies—since gradient computations are local to each layer—they still conform to the model below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, we assume that inputs and weights are fetched from main memory, and that each sublayer has sufficient local memory to store its outputs and weights either for a single sample (one datum per batch and one layer at a time) or for one channel across the entire batch. In general, intermediate tensors can have dimensions <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(\text{Channels}\,\times\,\text{Height}\,\times\,\text{Width}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Channels</mtext><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">×</mo><mtext>Height</mtext><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">×</mo><mtext>Width</mtext></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(\text{Channels}\,\times\,\text{Height}\,\times\,\text{Width}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> or
<math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(\text{Batch Size}\,\times\,\text{Height}\,\times\,\text{Width}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Batch Size</mtext><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">×</mo><mtext>Height</mtext><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">×</mo><mtext>Width</mtext></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(\text{Batch Size}\,\times\,\text{Height}\,\times\,\text{Width}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> (as <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\sim N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\sim N</annotation></semantics></math>).
This assumption is reasonable, since even a mid‑sized network requires only on the order of 2–3 MB of local memory.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To compute gradients for weight updates, we process each sample independently—reading one sample from memory, computing its gradient, and then averaging over the batch. This approach is broadly applicable, with one caveat for BatchNorm: computing the BatchNorm gradients requires the batch mean and variance, as well as the per‑sample BatchNorm output. However, this does not significantly increase memory traffic, because the batch statistics are computed during the forward pass and can be reused in the backward pass.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A2.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">B-A</span> </span><span id="A2.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backpropagation: Number of multiplications and memory accesses</span></h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">B-A</span>1 </span>Forward Pass(layer <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w\ast u^{(\ell-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w\ast u^{(\ell-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{ReLU}(z^{(\ell)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{ReLU}(z^{(\ell)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{u}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{u}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{max\_pool}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(a^{(\ell)}}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>pool</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{max\_pool}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(a^{(\ell)}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{BN}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\tilde{u}^{(\ell)}}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>BN</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{BN}\mathopen{}\mathclose{{\left(\tilde{u}^{(\ell)}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
